    "body": "## Motivation\n\nTwo bugs in `NDRotaryEmbedding` / `OneDRotaryEmbedding` (`multimodal_gen/runtime/layers/rotary_embedding/mrope.py`):\n\n1. `OneDRotaryEmbedding` ignores `theta_rescale_factor`. `build_freqs_outer` rescales a local `theta`, but `build_freqs` reads `self.theta`, so NTK rescaling never happens. With `theta_rescale_factor=4` the output is the same as with 1, and it does not match `get_1d_rotary_pos_embed` in the same file. This also affects `get_rotary_pos_embed(theta_rescale_factor=...)`.\n2. `NDRotaryEmbedding.forward_from_grid` crashes with `use_real=True, repeat_interleave_real=True`. The grid path allocates `sum(dims) // 2` columns while the 1D generator returns full-width slices:\n   `RuntimeError: The expanded size of the tensor (2) must match the existing size (4)`. `forward_uncached` handles this case already.\n\nNo in-tree caller hits either path today, so current models are unaffected.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `build_freqs` takes the rescaled `theta` from its caller.\n- `_forward_cached_from_grid` sizes outputs the same way `forward_uncached` does and takes each column width from the generator output.\n- Tests added to the existing `test_rope_complex_freqs_preconditions.py`: compare against `get_1d_rotary_pos_embed`, and check `forward_from_grid` matches `forward_uncached` on explicit positions.\n\n## Testing\n\nCPU, torch 2.14.1:\n- before the fix: the two new cases fail (`theta_rescale_factor=4.0`, `repeat_interleave_real=True`)\n- after: `5 passed, 4 subtests passed`\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #41848555939](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41848555939)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41848555951](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41848555951)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41848556219](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41848556219)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
